{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Six days.</b> The early authorities said: from the beginning of the sickle. It is possible that on the seventh day it is joined with the six days, and it separated it from one context to another to warn: you shall not do labor — and it did not say all labor. The meaning is all labor of service. And in the place where it said all labor, there it is written אך. And since it mentioned the Passover, which obligates coming to the place of glory, it mentioned the second festival and also the third, and did not mention the Day of Shofar-blast and the Day of the Tenth, for the community does not assemble at the Sanctuary."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The phrase 'from the beginning of the sickle' (מהחל חרמש) is Ibn Ezra's compressed paraphrase of a rabbinic interpretation deriving from Deut. 16:9; left hyper-literally as he wrote it."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:41.846241864Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}